+# Global Vocabulary Reconciliation
+
+**Audit branch:** `work/pre-m00-novel-assurance-redo-v3`
+**Gate:** pre-M00 novel assurance
+**Status:** PASS for this semantic unit
+
+## Reproduced defects
+
+1. The global synonym audit scanned machine-generated projection metadata headers as if they were human vocabulary. The admitted expected-red test reproduced candidate emission from projection schema, registry and namespace-scope header lines.
+2. After removing that scanner self-observation, 148 exact context-bound near-match occurrences remained unresolved under the occurrence-scoped vocabulary authority.
+
+## Repair
+
+- Extended the existing projection-header exclusion to all governed machine projection header prefixes. Human prose below the projection header remains scanned.
+- Added 148 occurrence-specific semantic dispositions to the PM-010 disposition register.
+- Every new disposition has `canonical_admission_effect=none` and `audit_resolution_effect=suppress_same_occurrence_only`.
+- No global aliases, canonical terms, namespace imports or broad path suppressions were added.
+
+## Evidence
+
+| Stage | Candidates | Resolved occurrences | Scanned files | Vocabulary touched |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| Fresh expected red | 151 | 1,228 | 537 | true |
+| After projection-header repair | 148 | 1,228 | 537 | true |
+| Final clean report | 0 | 1,376 | 537 | false |
+
+Validation:
+
+- Projection-header focused proof: `1 passed`.
+- Complete Tier A vocabulary suite: `105 passed in 21.20s`.
+- Global `--check-clean`: PASS, `candidates=0`, `resolved_occurrences=1376`.
+- Proof-block authority: `72/72` valid.
+- Tracked report and touch stamp match the final clean fingerprint.
+
+## Scope judgement
+
+The 148 remaining occurrences were implementation identifiers, test fixtures and negative evidence, configuration/control labels, or contextual human prose. Their exact-occurrence disposition prevents repeated false-positive review without changing the project vocabulary. This closes the global vocabulary gate without semantic expansion.
